    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nWhen recording a macro, the `<c-r>` and `<c-x>` triggers for mini.clue don't seem to be getting disabled, which is causing issues for me during macro playback.\r\n\r\nPasting the contents of the macro afterwards confirms that additional character codes are being inserted, so a `^R*` is actually being recorded as: `<80><fc>^DR*^R*`\r\n\r\nChecking `:verbose imap <c-r>` while running a macro also confirms that the key is still mapped.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\r\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath \"data\" .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n    vim.fn.system {\r\n        \"git\",\r\n        \"clone\",\r\n        \"--filter=blob:none\",\r\n        \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\",\r\n        \"--branch=stable\",\r\n        lazypath,\r\n    }\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup {\r\n    \"echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\r\n    version = false,\r\n    config = function()\r\n        local miniclue = require \"mini.clue\"\r\n        miniclue.setup {\r\n            triggers = {\r\n                -- Leader triggers\r\n                { mode = \"n\", keys = \"<Leader>\" },\r\n                { mode = \"x\", keys = \"<Leader>\" },\r\n\r\n                -- Built-in completion\r\n                { mode = \"i\", keys = \"<C-x>\" },\r\n\r\n                -- `g` key\r\n                { mode = \"n\", keys = \"g\" },\r\n                { mode = \"x\", keys = \"g\" },\r\n\r\n                -- Marks\r\n                { mode = \"n\", keys = \"'\" },\r\n                { mode = \"n\", keys = \"`\" },\r\n                { mode = \"x\", keys = \"'\" },\r\n                { mode = \"x\", keys = \"`\" },\r\n\r\n                -- Registers\r\n                { mode = \"n\", keys = '\"' },\r\n                { mode = \"x\", keys = '\"' },\r\n                { mode = \"i\", keys = \"<C-r>\" },\r\n                { mode = \"c\", keys = \"<C-r>\" },\r\n\r\n                -- Window commands\r\n                { mode = \"n\", keys = \"<C-w>\" },\r\n\r\n                -- `z` key\r\n                { mode = \"n\", keys = \"z\" },\r\n                { mode = \"x\", keys = \"z\" },\r\n            },\r\n\r\n            clues = {\r\n                -- Enhance this by adding descriptions for <Leader> mapping groups\r\n                miniclue.gen_clues.builtin_completion(),\r\n                miniclue.gen_clues.g(),\r\n                miniclue.gen_clues.marks(),\r\n                miniclue.gen_clues.registers(),\r\n                miniclue.gen_clues.windows(),\r\n                miniclue.gen_clues.z(),\r\n            },\r\n        }\r\n    end,\r\n}\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe mappings for `<c-r>` and `<c-x>` are cleared by mini.clue when beginning to record a macro, as is done with the other mini.clue mappings.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe keys are not being unmapped as expected.",
